Subject: [PATCH] One authority for the ten-gate pass, landed on the box that
 trades

The sealed judge began stamping an ELEVENTH stage, `swap_cost`, on every verdict
on 2026-09-14 (external_gauntlet.py:2455). `all_ten_pass` was a closed, ordered
tuple match, so from that day every certificate the judge minted was refused
SILENTLY by every downstream door -- including the sealed promoter, which calls
this predicate at promoter.py:1732. The authority file has held 174 attested rows
and the promoter has read 16 of them.

This lands the merged predicate: `gate_stage_census` reports what the judge
EMITTED against what policy REQUIRES, and `all_ten_pass` is its boolean. The ten
policy gates must each be present, be a mapping, carry `passed is True`, and
appear in policy order; EVERY extra stage must ALSO pass, so an unknown stage can
only ever refuse, never admit, and is published as UNRECOGNISED.

NO BAR MOVES. The judge already folds every stage it emits into its own top-level
verdict (external_gauntlet.py:2469), so a row the judge passed had already passed
its eleventh gate. Nothing is admitted that did not already pass ten gates; every
row re-admitted was judged and charged against multiplicity when it was minted, so
this has zero multiplicity effect. `fixed_trial_count` and
`fixed_variance_of_sharpes` are untouched. The `discovered` family stays banned.

Measured on this box: authority rows 174 attested, all_ten_pass 16 -> 174,
families 2 -> 7, and the sealed promoter's own load_cert_specs() 16 -> 174.

The box's copy was a byte-for-byte subset of this one: the merge diff is a single
hunk whose only removed lines are the seven-line old `all_ten_pass` body.

